{
  "version": "r0b-governance-v1",
  "rules": [
    "Public responses only use codes listed in public; unknown internal failures map to service_degraded.",
    "message is safe display text; it never echoes goal, background, title or artifact content.",
    "Worker-only database exceptions map to service_degraded on the public API and keep the raw code in internal logs.",
    "retryable means the same request may be resent unchanged: true only for 5xx and 429. preview_stale is not retryable; the client must create a new preview (recovery_action re_preview).",
    "db_exception_map lists every RAISE EXCEPTION code in r0a-schema-draft.sql (prefix before \":\"), including public codes raised verbatim; entries no longer raised are removed.",
    "Pre-existing guards that were never listed here keep the status their SQLSTATE fallback produced, so adopting this catalogue does not move a shipped response; a guard whose honest status differs is a separate decided change.",
    "Governance and resolution guards added after the R0a draft keep the status their SQLSTATE fallback produced, so registering them changes nothing observable; acceptance_blocked_unresolvable is defined by control design section 9 as a 409.",
    "Increments 0003-0016 raised 66 codes that were never listed here; they are now mapped to exactly what the SQLSTATE fallback already produced (48 to service_degraded, 18 to invalid_request), which is why no shipped response moved. The debt exemption list in the coverage guard is gone, so an unmapped raise can no longer slip through.",
    "The divergence among those 66 was resolved on 2026-11-02 by splitting the guard rather than re-stating one code: increment 0022 raises org_operator_suspended - public, 409, retryable false - when an operator suspended the organization, and keeps org_execution_disabled for status and execution_enabled states, which stay mapped to the retryable 503 they have always produced because those can change without a human acting. Control design section 9 still declares org_execution_disabled as a 409, and that row is about a different surface: the Host response to a seat grant that Work's POST /admin/seat-changes passes through at HTTP level, which never consults this map.",
    "Governance-integrity guards introduced after increment 0016 raise SQLSTATE 23514/22023, whose fallback would be 400 invalid_request, and are deliberately mapped to service_degraded instead: access_restriction_content_immutable, cancellation_intent_content_immutable, cancellation_intent_terminal_state, execution_entitlement_content_immutable, governance_change_content_immutable, governance_event_cursor_content_immutable, governance_gap_report_content_immutable, local_execution_policy_content_immutable, operation_resolution_content_immutable, operation_resolution_watermark_terminal, directory_protocol_invalid. None of them is reachable in a shipped surface (each first appears in 0018-0021, where production stands at 0016), and each reports either an attempt to rewrite state that is immutable by design or a Host event stream that does not match the closed contract. Neither is input the caller could fix by correcting a field: resending the same request gets the same refusal, so 400 would tell a client to repair something they had no part in. TestIncrementGuardsKeepTheirFallbackStatus requires any such deviation to be named in this file, so a mapping cannot drift away from the fallback quietly."
  ],
